.TH AENIGMA-TOR-AUTH 8 "2026-08-17" "aenigma 5.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Scripts"
.SH NAME
aenigma-tor-auth \- add v3 onion service client authorization for a user
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-tor-auth
.B \-s
.I SERVICE_NAME
.B \-u
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
.br
.B aenigma-tor-auth
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-tor-auth
generates a new x25519 client-authorization keypair for a v3 Tor onion
service previously configured with
.BR aenigma-tor (8),
installs the public half as an authorized client of that service, and
produces a ready-to-distribute private key file for the client.
.PP
The public key is written to
.IB AUTHORIZED_CLIENTS_DIR/ AUTHORIZED_USER .auth
in the format Tor expects for service-side authorization
(\fBdescriptor:x25519:<base32-public-key>\fR), granting that client access
once Tor is restarted. The private key is written to
.IB AUTHORIZED_CLIENTS_DIR/ AUTHORIZED_USER .auth_private
in the format Tor Browser and Tor clients expect for
.B ClientOnionAuthDir
credentials (\fB<onion-address>:descriptor:x25519:<base32-private-key>\fR),
so it can be copied as-is into a client's
.B ClientOnionAuthDir
without further editing. Tor is then restarted to apply the new
authorization.
.PP
.B aenigma-tor-auth
must be run as root, since it writes into
.IR /var/lib/tor ,
changes ownership of the generated key files, and restarts the
.B tor
systemd service. It requires that the named onion service has already
been configured and has finished publishing its address; see
.SM DIAGNOSTICS
below.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-s " SERVICE_NAME"
Name of the onion service to authorize the client for. Must match a
service already configured via
.BR aenigma-tor (8);
its service directory,
.IR /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME,
must already exist and contain a published
.I hostname
file. Required.
.TP
.BI \-u " AUTHORIZED_USER"
Identifier for the client being authorized, e.g. a username. Used as the
base filename for the generated
.I .auth
and
.I .auth_private
files. Required.
.TP
.B \-h
Display usage information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; the client keypair was generated, installed, and Tor was
restarted.
.TP
.B 1
Invoked without root privileges, called with insufficient or invalid
arguments, the named service directory does not exist, or the service's
.I hostname
file has not yet been generated.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME
Service directory created by
.BR aenigma-tor (8).
Must already exist.
.TP
.IB /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /hostname
The service's published onion address. Its content (minus the trailing
.B .onion
suffix) is embedded in the generated private key file. Must already exist.
.TP
.IB /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /authorized_clients
Directory holding one keypair per authorized client. Owned by
.IR debian-tor:debian-tor ,
mode 0700.
.TP
.IB /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /authorized_clients/ AUTHORIZED_USER .auth
Service-side public key file consumed by Tor to authorize the client.
Mode 0600.
.TP
.IB /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /authorized_clients/ AUTHORIZED_USER .auth_private
Client-side private key file, intended for secure out-of-band delivery to
the authorized client and placement in their
.B ClientOnionAuthDir
(or entry into Tor Browser's onion service authorization settings). Mode
0600.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
If
.IB /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME
does not exist,
.B aenigma-tor-auth
exits with an error instructing the operator to run
.BR aenigma-tor (8)
for that service first.
.PP
If the service directory exists but its
.I hostname
file is not yet present, Tor has not finished generating and publishing
the service's address.
.B aenigma-tor-auth
exits with an error rather than generating a private key file with a
missing or incorrect address; re-run once
.BR aenigma-tor (8)
reports the onion address.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Re-running
.B aenigma-tor-auth
for the same
.I SERVICE_NAME
and
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
generates a brand-new keypair and silently overwrites the existing
.I .auth
and
.I .auth_private
files. Any previously distributed private key for that user immediately
stops working once Tor is restarted, since only the new public key
remains installed as authorized.
.IP \(bu 2
The generated
.I .auth_private
file contains unencrypted key material. It should be transferred to the
authorized client over a secure, out-of-band channel and removed from the
server once delivered; it is not needed there for the service to keep
functioning.
.IP \(bu 2
.B umask 077
is set for the duration of the script, so intermediate files in its
working temporary directory are created with owner-only access before
being discarded.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aenigma-tor (8),
.BR openssl (1),
.BR tor (1),
.BR torrc (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.rujas@aenigma.ro>